## No-arbitrage check of the SVI fits (butterfly g(k) >= 0, not imposed)

- 48.8% of fitted expiries have g(k) < 0 somewhere on the grid ln(K/F) in [-0.5, 0.5] (wider if the quotes are), 3.8% inside their own quote range.
- 13.7% break Lee's wing bound b(1+|rho|) <= 2.
- Fits with a parameter on a fitting bound: 42.7%.
Violations mean the unconstrained-in-g SVI error is a slightly optimistic reference (the arbitrage-free SVI could only fit worse).

